      "content": "it's a bit polite, isn't it? even for a wealthy couple. i feel like they wouldn't be talking about \"chaos\" or \"security crumbling\" in such abstract ways. they'd be much more personal and pointed about it. i want them to express their actual disdain for the people they think are \"encroaching\" on their social status. can you make the dialogue more biting? i want them to really show that deep-seated sense of superiority they feel, maybe even mentioning their fear of having to actually interact with or witness \"them\" in their social circles. make it feel less like a political debate and more like the private, ugly thoughts of the upper class at the time.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
